sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-026: Administrative Content Moderation — Workflow Sequence
    actor Admin
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant ModerationService
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant Discovery
    participant Owner

    Admin->>ReactUI: Open Safety queue
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/admin/moderation/cases
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify Firebase token, MFA, active account, and stored ADMIN role
    alt Visitor, PART, suspended ADMIN, or role mismatch
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 401 or 403 with no-store response
        ReactUI-->>Admin: Denied or retry state
    else Authorized ADMIN
        ExpressAPI->>ModerationService: List cases newest first
        ModerationService->>PostgreSQL: Read moderation_cases
        PostgreSQL-->>ModerationService: Open, Dismissed, and Resolved cases
        ModerationService-->>ReactUI: Sanitized queue or empty state
    end

    Admin->>ReactUI: Open team, profile, or URL case
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/admin/moderation/cases
    ExpressAPI->>ModerationService: Validate target, HTTPS URL, and non-empty reason
    ModerationService->>PostgreSQL: Resolve target by target_type plus target_id
    PostgreSQL-->>ModerationService: Target exists or stale target
    alt Invalid input or missing target
        ModerationService-->>ReactUI: 400 or 404 and submitted draft
        ReactUI-->>Admin: Preserve entered values and show field errors
    else Valid target
        ModerationService->>PostgreSQL: Insert Open moderation case
        PostgreSQL-->>ReactUI: 201 case with created timestamp
    end

    Admin->>ReactUI: Choose dismiss, redact, warn, hide, or disable URL
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /cases/:caseId/decide with reason
    ExpressAPI->>ModerationService: Recheck ADMIN and Open case
    alt Missing, closed, or stale case
        ModerationService-->>ReactUI: 404 or 409 conflict
        ReactUI-->>Admin: Keep reason and reload current case
    else Open case
        ModerationService->>PostgreSQL: Apply selected content effect
        PostgreSQL-->>Discovery: Hidden team or profile excluded by discovery filters
        PostgreSQL-->>Owner: Persist warning, hidden, or URL-removal notification
        ModerationService->>PostgreSQL: Insert append-only safe action record
        ModerationService->>PostgreSQL: Mark case Dismissed or Resolved
        PostgreSQL-->>ModerationService: Updated case and UTC timestamps
        ModerationService-->>ReactUI: 200 outcome and scrubbed safe summary
        ReactUI-->>Admin: Success notice, refreshed case, and action history
    end

    Note over ModerationService,PostgreSQL: target_id is polymorphic. Application logic uses target_type to resolve a team or participant profile, and no physical target foreign key exists.
    Note over ModerationService,PostgreSQL: Content effect, notification, audit insert, and case closure are separate writes. Current code does not provide the atomic administrative mutation required by FR-079.
    Note over ReactUI,ModerationService: Credentials, OTPs, private contacts, and private workspace notes are scrubbed. Current DTOs still expose internal target IDs and a backend eventId on team detail.

